# pcsworld.ps2 - WORLD at the editor (`pcs 23`, the demo table, wset
# 5 3 3 4): each of the four sliders dragged somewhere new - one past the
# bottom (7), one past the top (0), two in between - a press that misses,
# QUIT, WORLD again and one more slide from beside its track, and the panel
# left UP so the bench reads every knob off the card (pcsworld.inc).
#
# ⚠ Card pixels.  WORLD is the tool column's icon at (564, 278).  The tracks
# are 28 wide from x 354 (GRAVITY, KICK) and 458 (SPEED, ELASTICITY), 136
# tall from y 48 and 264, and take a press 12 either side; a level is 16
# rows from the track's top + 4.  QUIT is (398..457, 432..455).
# checkpcs.py `ui-world` models every gesture from these points.
# ⚠ `origin 0 0`: that is where the pointer is when pcs starts.
origin 0 0
gap 300

# 1  WORLD: the panel
at 1.000    move to 564 278
+0.300      click left

# 2  GRAVITY past the bottom: 5 -> 7
at 5.000    move to 368 120
+0.300      down left
+0.300      move to 368 200
+0.300      move to 368 300
+0.400      up left

# 3  SPEED past the top: 3 -> 0
at 9.000    move to 472 100
+0.300      down left
+0.300      move to 472 40
+0.300      move to 472 4
+0.400      up left

# 4  KICK: down to 6 and back up to 2 before the release - 3 -> 2
at 13.000   move to 368 330
+0.300      down left
+0.300      move to 368 380
+0.300      move to 368 310
+0.400      up left

# 5  ELASTICITY, released wide of its track: the level is the release's y alone
at 17.000   move to 472 280
+0.300      down left
+0.300      move to 500 330
+0.300      move to 600 362
+0.400      up left

# 6  a press on the panel that is nothing: a miss
at 21.000   move to 330 470
+0.300      click left

# 7  QUIT
at 25.000   move to 420 444
+0.300      click left

# 8  WORLD again, GRAVITY from just beside its frame: 7 -> 4
at 29.000   move to 564 278
+0.300      click left
at 33.000   move to 345 100
+0.300      down left
+0.300      move to 345 125
+0.400      up left

at 38.000   type "q"
